From: perf session 2026-09-11
Subject: [PATCH 0028] icount: a timer re-armed beyond the running budget does not kick the vCPU

qemu_timer_notify_cb (the QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL timerlist notify) does
cpu_exit(current_cpu) whenever a timer_mod comes from the vCPU thread, so
that tcg_cpu_exec re-computes its icount budget.  On the pmb887x boot that
is 37k notifies/s: every timer_mod from a device MMIO callback and every
re-arm inside the idle warp's own timer run (0023) — and a temporary
counter showed only 1.2 % of them moved the deadline inside the remaining
budget.  Each needless exit_request cost an empty cpu_exec round
(EXCP_INTERRUPT) plus a TB_EXIT_REQUESTED unwind of the first TB.
Skip the kick when the new deadline (icount_round'ed) is not below the
insns left in the budget: the budget ends first and the loop recomputes.

Measured: dispatcher TB_EXIT_REQUESTED exits 554k -> 75k per boot (43 s
window); idlebench --quick vs base with 0023-0027: t1.3G 42.8 s (the
0023-0027 stack alone measured 42.2-43.8) — inside noise on its own, kept
on the counter.
Gates (with 0029): op-suite x4 identical, native suite 4/4 (branch
binary), lockstep 250e6 clean, Firefox idle, precise-clocks boot ok.

diff --git a/system/cpu-timers.c b/system/cpu-timers.c
--- a/system/cpu-timers.c	2026-09-11 11:52:09.756515676 +0000
+++ b/system/cpu-timers.c	2026-09-11 11:39:56.961362983 +0000
@@ -249,8 +249,26 @@
         /*
          * A CPU is currently running; send it out of the
          * tcg_cpu_exec() loop so it will recalculate its
-         * icount deadline immediately.
+         * icount deadline immediately - but only when the new deadline
+         * falls inside the budget it is running on.  A timer re-armed
+         * (or added) beyond the remaining budget cannot be missed: the
+         * budget ends first and the loop recomputes.  Measured on the
+         * pmb887x boot: 37k notifies/s on the vCPU thread (every
+         * timer_mod from a device callback or from the idle warp's own
+         * timer run), 1.2 % of them inside the budget - each needless
+         * exit_request cost an empty cpu_exec round plus a
+         * TB_EXIT_REQUESTED unwind of the first TB.
          */
+        if (icount_enabled()) {
+            CPUState *cpu = current_cpu;
+            int64_t deadline = qemu_clock_deadline_ns_all(QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL,
+                                                          QEMU_TIMER_ATTR_ALL);
+            int64_t left = cpu->neg.icount_decr.u16.low + cpu->icount_extra;
+
+            if (deadline >= 0 && icount_round(deadline) >= left) {
+                return;
+            }
+        }
         cpu_exit(current_cpu);
     } else if (first_cpu) {
         /*
